meta {
  name: Build Auth URL (reference)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{auth_url}}?client_id={{client_id}}&response_type=code&scope=com.intuit.quickbooks.accounting&redirect_uri={{redirect_uri}}&state=foundry-oauth-state
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  client_id: {{client_id}}
  response_type: code
  scope: com.intuit.quickbooks.accounting
  redirect_uri: {{redirect_uri}}
  state: foundry-oauth-state
}

docs {
  This is a reference request — do not execute it directly.
  Open the URL in a browser to start the OAuth flow.
  QBO will redirect to redirect_uri with ?code=...&realmId=...

  In Foundry, AuthURL() in client.go builds this URL.
  The /integrations/qbo/connect handler redirects the user here.

  Bug fixed 2026-07-09: the url field previously had no query string —
  only the params:query{} block, which Bruno treats as a display mirror
  of the url's own query string, not an independent source. Sending it
  produced a bare https://appcenter.intuit.com/connect/oauth2 with zero
  params, which is why Intuit rejected it as "client_id missing" even
  with client_id correctly set in the environment.
}
